From Rohan, great opportinity!
&gt; For anyone in Berkeley/SF: *Sebastian Prasanna and I are running a Risk Report Review Workshop this weekend at Constellation.* Arrow (a new AI safety org started by Francis Rhys Ward) is collecting data (that may be used for METR's Time Horizon 2.0) and needs people to a) review frontier model model cards and b) grade those model card reviews.
&gt; 
&gt; Participants will be paid $540 per day (up to 30 participants, which we likely won't hit). This is also useful for you to see what these risk reports and model cards say and to form views about what kinds of evidence justify claims of model safety.
&gt; 
&gt; If you can't make both days, we'd still appreciate if you can join for one day, or even half a day. Just specify which day you will join when you RSVP. Sorry for the short notice: we may have to cancel if we get fewer than 10 people. (But we're pretty sure we can get at least 10, we're already close.)
&gt; 
&gt; *Please sign up at this partiful soon if you're interested!*  <https://partiful.com/e/5hQITg4oRWbcOTvt53KA?c=pXFxstcE|partiful.com/e/…?c=pXFxstcE>

